    <h2>How to use this</h2>
    <p>If you just want the short version, the Cuties profile is enough. This is for if you want to know what you're walking into.</p>
    <h2>Me</h2>
    <p>I've been playing professional poker for about twenty years. I'm somewhere between still being a pro and being retired. I still play and I still make money. I just don't need to anymore. I host a game semi-regularly. It's profitable, but I do it because I like it. It rains money on the people around me. Waitresses, dealers, girls who work the game, they all make a lot of money here.</p>
    <p>I've been dating from that crowd because it's easy. These women come into my orbit and they're easy to date. I'm not looking for one of those girls anymore. Whatever girl lands in my life is probably going to fall somewhere in this orbit anyway. I want you choosing that, not because it's your job to be in the room.</p>
    <p>I also have a life outside of poker. I hike a lot. There's a good trail nearby, Martin Canyon Creek. I play pickleball all the time. I used to be a collegiate tennis player until my shoulders got too messed up. I'd love to find a girl who joins me for that. I play pinball two or three times a week.</p>
    <h2>What I want</h2>
    <p>I want to rip a girl out of her own life and stick her in mine. A real one. Not a visitor.</p>
    <h2>Sex</h2>
    <p>What I really want is something close to a free-use partner, more than CNC. The best relationships I've had were with girls who describe themselves as good girls. Quite a few of them have called me daddy and I kind of like that. I want a girl who doesn't say no because she has no reason to. High sex drive, wants me all the time, we're going to have a good time. I have a high sex drive too, so I become incompatible with women who only want it three or four times a week. I don't need the CNC. I also don't mind training a brat to be a good girl.</p>
    <h2>If our beliefs fight</h2>
    <p>I don't think we have the technology to change sex yet. If a person registers as male to me and tells me he is a woman, I register that he believes interesting things about himself. I don't change my mind, and I don't like using pronouns I don't believe. I tend to just disengage. If that's a problem, this won't work, and that's fine.</p>
    <h2>Practical</h2>
    <p>East Bay. I go out. I'm not hard to meet. I'm going to Slutcon in September. If you want to meet there, say so.</p>
